Patch-ID: P-APP-001 (wave-5 slice 3) — readiness signaling, ScopedKeepAlive
and profile-registration seams (scaffolding only, no real profile work).
Rationale: fourth milestone of engine/docs/patches/P-APP-001.md. Ships the
bridge-side seams the remaining lifecycle work hangs off, all gated on
rearc::GetEngineLifecycleHost() so stock behavior stays bit-identical with
the gate off:
- Readiness: additive rearc_readiness.{h,cc} defines EngineReadinessSink +
  SetEngineReadinessSink() + SignalEngineReady(). A new
  ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::PostBrowserStart() override signals after the
  base implementation — the spec's "async profile unblocking and
  PostBrowserStart" tail of PreMainMessageLoopRunImpl
  (chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main.cc:2163-2165). The sink is standalone
  rather than an EngineLifecycleHost extension so this patch stays purely
  additive over app/002's files; it merges into the lifecycle host C ABI
  surface in the shell-integration wave. framework.exports/framework.order
  are deliberately untouched (per wave-5 scope): no new exported symbols.
- Keepalive: additive rearc_keep_alive.{h,cc} wraps ScopedKeepAlive
  (components/keep_alive_registry) as AcquireShellKeepAlive() /
  ReleaseShellKeepAlive() / HasShellKeepAlive(), mirroring AppController's
  APP_CONTROLLER/DISABLED keepalive (app_controller_mac.mm:824). Scaffolding
  only: no call sites yet; acquisition joins the readiness C ABI wave and
  release joins ordered bridge finalization (P-APP-001 steps 3 and 6).
- Profile registration: additive rearc_profile_registry.{h,cc} records opaque
  Profile handles (forward-declared; the bridge's consumers must not need the
  full browser target). A gated call in
  ChromeBrowserMainPartsMac::PostProfileInit() registers each profile as
  Chromium brings it up. No prefs, KeyedServices, session-restore or
  startup-window interaction — no real profile work.
Build wiring: the six seam sources join source_set("core")'s is_mac block in
chrome/browser/BUILD.gn (with //components/keep_alive_registry in the deps'
//components group) instead of app/002's rearc_bridge target. Rationale:
every patch in the series must individually pass `git apply --check -R`
against the fully applied tree, and a new-file patch (002) cannot
reverse-apply once its created files carry later modifications — so app/005
never touches app/002's files. Both BUILD.gn hunks sit >10 lines from 002's
deps hunk. Fold the sources back into rearc_bridge at the next pin rebase,
when the patch set is refreshed as a whole.
Placement notes (same reverse-apply invariant): the two rearc_bridge includes
sit outside the alphabetical include group and the PostBrowserStart override
is declared/defined out of stage order, keeping this patch's hunks clear of
app/003's include-hunk and app/004's DidEndMainMessageLoop-hunk -U3 context
windows. Regroup include/stage order at the next pin rebase.
Gate history: attempt 1 (superseded) extended app/002's rearc_engine_lifecycle
and rearc_bridge/BUILD.gn directly and compiled green, but broke app/002's
git apply --check -R; this restructured patch replaces it. Both attempts'
compile logs are in engine/build-p5.log.
